@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.10
@changelog
  - Codename: Prettyyyyy... Prettyyyyy... Pretty Good!
  - Folder Mode learns nested folders: long-press SEL spills the full ancestor chain, collapse keeps descendant spill state so re-spilling the top instantly restores the drill-down.
  - New Temporary Selection Set parallel to the 8 named slots — built-ins temp_selset_add / _remove / _recall / _scroll. Mutually exclusive with the 1..8 slot recall.
  - UC1 Encoder 1 (CHANNEL) now fully bindable like Encoder 2. Default Plain = new built-in track_scroll (visible-track scroll + select + UC1 focus follow). Shift = instance_cycle.
  - New built-in bc_track_scroll_select: same scroll as bc_track_scroll but also pulls REAPER selection + UF8 bank to the new BC anchor. Original bc_track_scroll unchanged.
  - FX Learn user fader label now appears on the UF8 scribble's upper line, not just in the value-line fallback.
  - Release codenames: extension/version-names.tsv maps each tag to a codename, shown on the About tab below the version line.
  - Persistence rebuilt: Selection Set slots + Temp set saved into the project RPP via the official projectconfig SDK hook. Old SetProjExtState path was silently dropping writes on some REAPER builds.
